---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Seriatim — a macOS generative instrument"
  description="Seriatim is a macOS VST3/AU generative instrument that composes four-voice music that never repeats, for roughly 931 million events per voice."
  ogImage="/media/seriatim-demo-poster.jpg"
>
  <h1>Seriatim</h1>
  <p>
    An instrument that composes four-voice music that never repeats — for
    roughly 931 million events per voice before it does.
  </p>

  <video
    controls
    playsinline
    poster="/media/seriatim-demo-poster.jpg"
    class="w-full rounded-brand"
  >
    <source src="/media/seriatim-demo.webm" type="video/webm" />
    <source src="/media/seriatim-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
  </video>

  <h2>The number that makes the point</h2>
  <p>
    Seriatim generates each voice from a twelve-tone row driven by six
    coprime periods (576, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19). Their least common
    multiple — <strong>576 × 5 × 7 × 11 × 13 × 17 × 19 = 931,170,240</strong> —
    is how many events pass before that voice's combined state repeats. At
    any reasonable tempo, that's longer than a lifetime of continuous
    listening.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>VST3, AU, AU MIDI FX, and a standalone app</li>
    <li>Universal binary — Apple silicon and Intel</li>
    <li>Built-in 4-voice synthesis, or MIDI out on channels 1–4 or MPE</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <p>macOS 11.0 or later. Apple silicon or Intel.</p>

  <p><Button href="/seriatim/download">Download Seriatim</Button></p>
</Base>
